  "sources": [
    {
      "title": "Andy Burnham promises ‘serious dialogue’ over UK’s relationship with EU",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/politics/2026/oct/12/andy-burnham-britain-eu-brexit-reset",
      "description": "<p>PM hails next month’s ‘reset’ summit as first step to closer ties, but tensions over trade may prove problematic</p><p>Andy Burnham has promised a “serious dialogue” over the UK’s future place in Europe, saying the existing relationship is “not good enough” as he framed next month’s Brussels summit as a possible first step to EU membership.</p><p>The prime minister said Britain must take a “clear-eyed rational look” at its long-term relationship with the bloc to boost economic growth and control immigration, which needed to go beyond Labour’s existing red lines.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/politics/2026/oct/12/andy-burnham-britain-eu-brexit-reset\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-10-12T19:15:11"
    },
    {
      "title": "Burnham says ‘public will be the boss’ in any future decision about closer relationship with the EU – as it happened",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/politics/live/2026/oct/12/uk-politics-live-tories-andy-burnham-russian-interference-brexit-eu-latest",
      "description": "<p>The prime minister tells MPs the next summit with the EU will be held on 20 November</p><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/politics/2026/oct/12/burnham-urge-mps-embrace-closer-ties-with-eu\">Burnham to urge MPs to embrace closer ties with EU</a></p><p><strong>Zia Yusuf</strong>, Reform UK’s home affairs spokesperson, is speaking now. He started his speech with an account of a 73-year-old woman dying in North Wales after having to wait 23 hours for an ambulance, and he sought to link this to immigration.</p><p>He said:</p><p>The Royal College of Emergency Medicine estimates that 15,000 people across Britain died last year due to excess wait times for emergency treatment. That’s 300 people a week, 300 lives destroyed, 300 families devastated.</p><p>And that number has increased tenfold over the last decade. This is a moral outrage, and it is a direct result of decisions made by Tory and Labour governments.</p><p>I don’t think that’s because he wants to have a fight over the European Union. I think that’s because he knows what we’re talking about today impacts hard in what is known as the red wall.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/politics/live/2026/oct/12/uk-politics-live-tories-andy-burnham-russian-interference-brexit-eu-latest\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-10-12T17:34:40"
    },
